    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> ilyas-mallah created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14897#discussion_r4339321083\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Makes sense, SIMD stays enabled by default and <code>build_compiler</code> now only errors when the compiler can't do it, with its signature unchanged. The docs say it has to be combined with <code>has_v</code> or disabled, and the riscv64 disas tests turn SIMD off in the harness: <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/commit/c1c52260d277ded405f3f9264a0c02ee73b766c3\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/commit/c1c52260d277ded405f3f9264a0c02ee73b766c3</a></p>\n<p>If you'd rather have that in the test files, I can put the flags in <code>make-load-store-tests.sh</code> and the other riscv64 disas tests instead.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633707864,
