    },
    {
        "content": "<p>ilyas-mallah updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14897\">PR #14897</a>.</p>",
        "id": 634133981,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792709457
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>ilyas-mallah <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14897#issuecomment-6353055452\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14897\">PR #14897</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You were right, it's from this change. <code>checks_incompatible_target</code> builds an engine for the host's triple with an unknown OS, which under QEMU is a riscv64 target without <code>has_v</code>, so <code>Engine::new</code> now fails on the SIMD check before the mismatch error it looks for. The test turns off SIMD and relaxed SIMD for its engines: <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/commit/bd2961f13a6329934957bbbf3e6adcc7bb4f2211\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/commit/bd2961f13a6329934957bbbf3e6adcc7bb4f2211</a></p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 634134028,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792709470
